# Single source of truth for the we-are-mono/ASK commit used by:
#   - kernel patches (kernel/flavors/ask/patches/, via
#     kernel/common/scripts/sync-ask-kernel.sh)
#   - OOT kernel modules (cdx.ko, fci.ko, auto_bridge.ko) and userspace
#     daemons (cmm, dpa_app), via bin/ci-build-ask-modules.sh /
#     bin/ci-build-ask-userspace.sh
# Bump ASK_VERSION here only, so kernel + modules + userspace can never
# drift apart from each other again (see plans/enumerated-forging-pie.md,
# finding #1: this repo previously had the kernel side on ASK's now-deleted
# `fix/security-hardening` branch while modules/userspace were pinned to
# `mt-6.12.y` @ a211ea8 -- two different, un-cross-checked refs).
#
# 2026-09-11: bumped to the same commit currently live on
# we-are-mono/openwrt's `mono` branch (package/ask/ask-version.mk),
# confirmed fetchable (not dangling). Re-synced together via
# sync-ask-kernel.sh + a full patch-apply/build/hardware validation pass
# (Phase 2 of the plan above) -- this is not a blind pin bump.
ASK_REPO=https://github.com/we-are-mono/ASK.git
ASK_VERSION=5d96de360d8ec7809d8b97cee0ad591e48c5e73e
